import{_ as e,o,c as a,ao as d}from"./chunks/framework.CSb4BAU4.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Outputs and layout","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"outputs.md","filePath":"outputs.md","lastUpdated":null}'),i={name:"outputs.md"};function r(l,t,n,s,c,h){return o(),a("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[d('<h1 id="Outputs-and-layout" tabindex="-1">Outputs and layout <a class="header-anchor" href="#Outputs-and-layout" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Outputs and layout {#Outputs-and-layout}&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="Inputs" tabindex="-1">Inputs <a class="header-anchor" href="#Inputs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Inputs {#Inputs}&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:right;">case</th><th style="text-align:right;">LDA</th><th style="text-align:right;">GGA</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:right;">restricted</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>ρ</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>ρ, σ</code> with σ = ∇ρ·∇ρ</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">polarized</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>(ρα, ρβ)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>(ρα, ρβ), (σαα, σαβ, σββ)</code> with σαβ = ∇ρα·∇ρβ</td></tr></tbody></table><p>ρ and the σ components are numbers of any <code>Real</code> type; the result type is the promotion of the functional&#39;s number type and the input types.</p><h2 id="Output-names" tabindex="-1">Output names <a class="header-anchor" href="#Output-names" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Output names {#Output-names}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>xc_derivatives(f, Val(k), ...)</code> returns a <code>NamedTuple</code> with the energy per volume <code>e</code> (e = ρ·ε, not Libxc&#39;s energy per particle <code>zk</code>; <a href="/PureAtomistic.jl/PureXC/dev/api#PureXC.zk"><code>zk</code></a> converts) and one field for each split a + b = j of each order j = 1, …, k, with a descending: a derivatives in the densities and b in the σ components. The field is named <code>v[j]rho[a]sigma[b]</code>, with each exponent written only when it is above 1 and each part left out when its count is 0:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:right;">order</th><th style="text-align:right;">LDA</th><th style="text-align:right;">GGA</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:right;">0</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>e</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>e</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">1</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>vrho</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>vrho</code>, <code>vsigma</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">2</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>v2rho2</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>v2rho2</code>, <code>v2rhosigma</code>, <code>v2sigma2</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">3</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>v3rho3</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>v3rho3</code>, <code>v3rho2sigma</code>, <code>v3rhosigma2</code>, <code>v3sigma3</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;">j</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>vjrhoj</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>vjrhoj</code>, <code>vjrho(j-1)sigma</code>, …, <code>vjsigmaj</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>These are Libxc&#39;s names, so code moving from Libxc needs no renaming; Libxc provides orders 0 to 2.</p><h2 id="Polarized-layout" tabindex="-1">Polarized layout <a class="header-anchor" href="#Polarized-layout" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Polarized layout {#Polarized-layout}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A restricted field is a number. A polarized field is a tuple over the density multisets of size a, in lexicographic order over (α, β), each followed in turn by the σ multisets of size b in lexicographic order over (αα, αβ, ββ). This is Libxc&#39;s order:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:right;">field</th><th style="text-align:right;">components</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>vrho</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">α, β</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>vsigma</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">αα, αβ, ββ</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>v2rho2</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">αα, αβ, ββ</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>v2rhosigma</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">α·αα, α·αβ, α·ββ, β·αα, β·αβ, β·ββ</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>v2sigma2</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">αα·αα, αα·αβ, αα·ββ, αβ·αβ, αβ·ββ, ββ·ββ</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>v3rho3</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">ααα, ααβ, αββ, βββ</td></tr></tbody></table><p>A field of a densities and b σ components has binomial(a + 1, a)·binomial(b + 2, b) components.</p><h2 id="Array-layout" tabindex="-1">Array layout <a class="header-anchor" href="#Array-layout" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Array layout {#Array-layout}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The array layer takes the inputs of all points at once:</p><ul><li><p>restricted: vectors <code>ρ</code> (and <code>σ</code>) with the same axes;</p></li><li><p>polarized: a <code>2 × n</code> matrix <code>ρ</code> and a <code>3 × n</code> matrix <code>σ</code>, the spin on dimension 1 in the order above and the points on dimension 2.</p></li></ul><p>Every output field is a matrix with one row per component of the field (one row for a scalar field) and the point axis of the inputs as its columns. <a href="/PureAtomistic.jl/PureXC/dev/api#PureXC.xc_outputs"><code>xc_outputs</code></a> allocates them with <code>similar</code>, so the array type and the point axis follow <code>ρ</code>, including the offset axes of an <code>OffsetArray</code>.</p>',16)])])}const p=e(i,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,p as default};
